meta {
  name: Events - Create - Time that does not exist
  type: http
  seq: 189
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/spaces/<cuid of an events space>/events
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Night session",
    "starts_at": "2027-03-28T02:30:00+01:00",
    "ends_at": "2027-03-28T04:00:00+02:00",
    "time_zone": "Europe/Brussels"
  }
}

docs {
  Error case: on 28 March 2027 the clocks of Brussels go from 02:00 to 03:00, so 02:30 does not exist: 400 on starts_at, "This time does not exist in this zone. Choose 01:59 or earlier, or 03:00 or later." A time that exists twice (31 October 2027, 02:30) is accepted with +02:00 or +01:00: the offset decides the instant.
}
